From: McFredward <frederik@lissek.info>
Subject: [PATCH] hevc: omit unused Main8/420 chroma reconstruction in explicit gray mode

Local R8-mask optimization, LGPL-2.1-or-later. Applied after the independent-NAL
slice backport. Only an explicit AV_CODEC_FLAG_GRAY with Main8/420 opts in.
Keep chroma syntax, entropy, residual parsing, neighbor metadata and complete
luma reconstruction/filtering. Chroma planes are unspecified in this mode and
must never be sampled. Other profiles and normal color decoding remain intact.

